%I A400823 #16 Nov 10 2026 13:18:41
%S A400823 0,0,0,10,72,484,3404,25022,189412,1459048,11350648,88785554
%N A400823 Number of Type C megastars of generation 1 (single minor star triples, MC(1)) in the level-n supertile of the Spectre tiling.
%C A400823 The level-n supertile is obtained from a single Spectre tile by n inflation steps of the S8/S9 substitution and contains A057080(n) tiles. A star triple is a set of three Spectre tiles related by a rotation through 120 degrees about a common point of their boundaries.
%C A400823 Star triples arise on the seams of the inflation steps and form clusters there. The clusters are chains of three kinds of megaobjects: Type A megastars (A397120), Type C megastars (A400810) and Type A palindromes (A400811).
%C A400823 The Type C megastar of generation g, MC(g), has A400810(g) star triples. MC(1) is a single minor star triple; MC(g) for g >= 2 has a minor star triple at its center and three arms, related by rotations through 120 degrees about the center. Each arm is a copy of the Family C cluster of generation g-1 (A397116), that is, a chain of Type A palindromes PA(1), ..., PA(g-1). MC(g) is created at level g+2 and afterwards only copied.
%C A400823 Therefore the same sequence counts the copies of every generation: the level-n supertile contains a(n) copies of MC(1), a(n-1) copies of MC(2), a(n-2) copies of MC(3), and in general a(n-g+1) copies of MC(g), for 1 <= g <= n-2. Every Type C megastar appears in 10 copies at the level where it is created, in 72 copies one level later, in 484 two levels later, and so on.
%C A400823 The number of star triples in all Type C megastars of the level-n supertile is A400821(n) = Sum_{g=1..n-2} A400810(g)*a(n-g+1).
%C A400823 a(0)-a(7) were obtained by direct counts in the level-n supertiles. The other terms and the formulas follow from the growth rules of the clusters and megaobjects; they are not proved.
