%H A400823 David Smith, Joseph Samuel Myers, Craig S. Kaplan, and Chaim Goodman-Strauss, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17743">A chiral aperiodic monotile</a>, arXiv:2305.17743 [math.CO], 2023-2024.
%F A400823 Conjecture: a(n) = 13*a(n-1) - 44*a(n-2) + 28*a(n-3) + 5*a(n-4) - a(n-5) for n >= 6.
%F A400823 Conjectured g.f.: 2*x^3*(1 - 6*x)*(5 + x)/((1 - x)*(1 - 8*x + x^2)*(1 - 4*x - x^2)).
%F A400823 Conjecture: a(n) = 6*A001090(n-2) - A001090(n-3) + (A033887(n-1) - 5)/2 for n >= 3.
%F A400823 Limit_{n->oo} a(n)/A057080(n) = (133*sqrt(15) - 515)/10 = 0.0106785045... (one MC(1) for every (133*sqrt(15) + 515)/11 = 93.6460713... tiles).
%F A400823 Conjecture: the number of Type C megastars of all generations in the level-n supertile is Sum_{m=3..n} a(m) = (5*A001090(n-1) + A001090(n-2))/6 + A014445(n)/4 - 5*n/2 + 13/6 for n >= 3 (10, 82, 566, 3970, ...); its limit ratio to A057080(n) is (9 - sqrt(15))/(6*(35 + 9*sqrt(15))) = 0.0122322... (one Type C megastar for every (450 + 116*sqrt(15))/11 = 81.751... tiles).
%e A400823 a(3) = 10: the level-3 supertile (559 tiles) contains 28 star triples, 18 major and 10 minor (A400813(3), A400814(3)); each of the 10 minor star triples is a Type C megastar of generation 1.
%e A400823 a(4) = 6*8 - 1 + (55 - 5)/2 = 72.
%e A400823 The level-5 supertile contains a(5) = 484 copies of MC(1), a(4) = 72 copies of MC(2) and a(3) = 10 copies of MC(3), together 566 Type C megastars with 484*1 + 72*7 + 10*37 = 1358 = A400821(5) star triples.
%t A400823 CoefficientList[Series[2 x^3 (1 - 6 x) (5 + x)/((1 - x) (1 - 8 x + x^2) (1 - 4 x - x^2)), {x, 0, 23}], x]
